# camera-demo

PICO-Cam-A live HM01B0 preview on the ST7789V LCD. Starts paused with AREA
sampling selected. K3 (active-low GP18) starts/stops capture. Stop places the
sensor in standby and retains the displayed image. K4 (active-low GP19)
cycles NEAREST, AREA, AREA+TIME; it works while running or paused. The top
17 LCD rows show the state, selected mode, and button actions.

NEAREST selects one source pixel per destination pixel. AREA averages the
fractional source-pixel areas covering each destination pixel. AREA+TIME adds
an exponential temporal average: half the new AREA sample plus half the
previous output. It reduces random noise but can leave trails on moving
objects. History resets on start and mode changes. Eight startup frames are
discarded on each start to give automatic exposure time to settle; this is
not a guarantee of convergence in every lighting condition. No sensor gain,
exposure, or register settings are changed by K4.

Buttons use falling-edge latches so a tap during synchronous capture is
retained. One action per press, with 30 ms of observed release before the
next press is accepted; a button held at boot must first be released.
Actions take effect between frames. Camera-linked firmware uses a 200 MHz system clock and 1.15 V core supply
from startup; stopping capture retains that clock. Capture has a 500 ms deadline. ERR3,
ERR4, and ERR8 mean initialization, capture, and standby failure; K3 retries
from a stopped state. Fatal exit codes: 2 display initialization, 5 geometry,
6 pixel/text transfer, 7 refresh, 9 GPIO/timer operation. Resources are
released on fatal exits.

preview.h and test/preview.cpp are application code written for modules.cpp,
not copied from ArduCAM or Waveshare. The test covers sampling, averaging
history and button debounce/edge retention without camera hardware:

```sh
sh apps/camera-demo/test/run.sh
```
